@* Hidden returnUrl for a POST form: the page the form is on, so the action can send the user back
   (the controller only follows local URLs, see RedirectToLocal).
   When a failed POST re-shows a page (Task/Create re-shows the Tasks page), the request path is the
   POST's URL, so the controller passes the original page in ViewData["ReturnUrl"]; that wins. *@
<input type="hidden" name="returnUrl"
       value="@(ViewData["ReturnUrl"] as string ?? $"{Context.Request.Path}{Context.Request.QueryString}")" />
